query Props($input: ProposalsInput!) {
  proposals(input: $input) {
    nodes { ... on Proposal {
      id onchainId status quorum createdAt chainId
      governor { id }
      start { ... on Block { number timestamp } ... on BlocklessTimestamp { timestamp } }
      end { ... on Block { number timestamp } ... on BlocklessTimestamp { timestamp } }
      voteStats { type votesCount votersCount percent }
      events { type createdAt }
      metadata { title description }
    } }
    pageInfo { lastCursor }
  }
}

metadata.description:
# INT Audit with Guardian
As discussed in the governance [post](https://gov.theinternettoken.com/t/int-audit-with-guardian/66) INT airdrop contract is almost finished and before it is deployed and configured we would need to do an audit.&#x20;

The idea is to engage reputable firm [Guardian Audits](https://guardianaudits.com/) to audit both the new contracts as well as the existing INT code base and get up to speed in making sure our INT project is safe and secure. This also helps us to be ready to audit only incremental changes for all future feature upgrades.&#x20;

The pricing model which is most applicable for us in the situation is the Price Per Vulnerability model from their available pricing options.&#x20;
The PPV model cost is
\= Base(15K per week) + ppv(C, H, M).

It is estimated that audit will take one week and we have gotten an invoice confirmation from Guardian for $15K. You can find the invoice [here](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1y4ytDPgTCR72OlNyJReuIBidBvY_oozx/view?usp=sharing)

This vote is to get approval from DAO for this effort. To fund this effort 6 WETH will be moved to multisig. Multisig then will exchange the necessary WETH to USDC before doing the transfer to Guardian to the address mentioned in the invoice.&#x20;

Please kindly review and vote accordingly.&#x20;

PS: There would be a separate vote for actual deployment of airdrop contract where we will have full audit report along with more information on deployment config etc.&#x20;

# IFT Rewards and Airdrop
This proposal is to get official ratification from DAO on implementing the following short term reward program for IFT holders. Details can be found here in this governance forum.&#x20;

<https://gov.theinternettoken.com/t/proposal-ift-rewards-airdrops/47>

Duration: 24 weeks. (March 22nd to Sep 6th) Program is back-filled starting from launch date.&#x20;

Budget: 9.72 million INT

Weekly emission cap: 500K INT

Target Implementation timeline: Mid June

Implementation Budget: TBD (Based on the quotes from Dev and QA)

There is no on-chain executable action yet associated to this proposal as we still have to build the solution.&#x20;

The main purpose of this proposal&#x20;

* To get this officially ratified by DAO, so we can share this publicly that we are committing funds for this program and commence planning activities
* Reach out to dev community to get quotes, design and build the solution.&#x20;
* Also have QA/audits lined up

Implementation costs will be fulfilled by Operations funding(assuming that vote passes). If costs of implementation are over $15K then Operations team will create a separate proposal to get explicit approval for implementation budget
